Z||000001||beer_stud_21||09-08-2001||03:35 AM||||I'm not positive that you do need the decoder card.  I will have to look it up.  The early Wallstreet era PB's needed the decoder card for DVD, and they eventually moved to software decoding.  So how did you end up with a DVD drive and no decoder card?  You should either have a decoder PCMCIA card with the DVD drive or you dont need one.  Let me look up the specs on your 333 Lombard to make sure.  If your PB is meant to use sotfware decoding you need to download the Apple DVD Player that is meant to do software decoding.  It is different than the one that does the decoding in hardware.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
